WEBVTT

NOTE Actual full-workspace tutorial recording. Prepared starter QA account; five later phases explicitly opened. No earned passes, AI, execution, edits or submissions. Normal speed; no added holds.

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:07.320
1 of 6. Write the test suite
Open Write tests and choose an editable test file. Cover the required behavior and edge cases from the brief, then check that your work has saved.

2
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:13.440
2 of 6. Run and inspect the tests
Run tests executes the suite when the runner is available. Open Execution evidence to read the actual output. A failed or unavailable run needs attention before it can support your review.

3
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:19.640
3 of 6. Challenge your tests with planted bugs
Open Test coverage to inspect which planted bugs the suite detects. Use the available run control when you choose to test it; a surviving bug points to behavior your assertions may not cover.

4
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:25.840
4 of 6. Keep the brief close
Show brief to revisit the task and review criteria. Show mentor opens optional guidance. You can hide either panel to make space; your work and conversations stay in their own phase.

5
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:31.800
5 of 6. Submit tests with their evidence
Submit your saved tests for review and read the recorded feedback. Strengthen assertions that miss behavior, then check and submit again. An empty evidence view is not a passing result.

6
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:37.640
6 of 6. Return whenever you need help
Replay tutorial brings these steps back. Optional phase guide opens the lessons. In the workspace mentor, Guided offers hints. Agentic proposes changes: compare them, explain this exact version in your own words, then choose Apply only if your explanation is accepted. A changed proposal needs a new explanation.
